From fff919890f9e7d130666010b3956647cf134becd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:24:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Teaching Loops: punchy ~2 minute topic-teaching video,
 recorded in-browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same technique as QuoteLoopRecorder/PastQuestionLoopRecorder — canvas +
Web Audio API + MediaRecorder, entirely client-side. No Remotion, no
video_scripts, no laptop render worker: nothing renders until an admin
opens /admin/teaching-loops and clicks Record, same as every other Loop.

- lib/content-factory/generators/teaching-loop.js: LLM prompt for a
  10-14 card script (hook -> why it matters -> teach it -> common mistake
  -> recap -> CTA), each card short enough to read on-screen since this
  is a silent video (background music only, no voiceover) + a
  word-count-based hold-time estimator scaled to ~2 minutes total.
- app/api/admin/teaching-loops/generate: generates the script and picks
  ONE background candidate (stock video, falls back to photo) for the
  whole clip, same fallback helper quote-loops/generate already uses.
- app/api/admin/teaching-loops/list: scoped list w/ media_files, same
  pattern as quote-loops/list.
- app/api/admin/teaching-loops/save: uploads the recorded blob's URL
  into media_files, marks the draft approved, auto-queues publish jobs
  in the background — same pattern as quote-loops/save.
- components/TeachingLoopRecorder.js: draws an Instagram-Stories-style
  progress bar + one text card at a time over a continuous
  Ken-Burns-zoomed background, fading through the whole script, records
  with MediaRecorder.
- app/admin/teaching-loops/page.js: pick topic -> generate -> Record ->
  Publish to Channels, same layout as /admin/quote-loops.
- components/AdminSidebar.js: nav entry.

Needs a 'teaching-loops' bucket in Supabase storage (public read,
authenticated upload — same policy shape as quote-loops) before first
save.
